<report>
<title>Normal distribution (z) test - two independent samples</title>
<br />
<block name="sample">
<table>
<tr><td>Sample name:</td><td><in>name</in></td></tr>
<tr><td>Mean = </td><td><in>mean</in></td></tr>
<tr><td>Variance =</td><td><in>var</in></td></tr>
<tr><td>Size =</td><td><in>size</in></td></tr>
</table>
<br />
</block>
<p>Combined standard error = <in>error</in></p>

<p><ci><in>pc</in>% confidence interval for difference between means = <in>from</in> to <in>to</in></ci></p>

<p>Standard normal deviate (z) = <in>z</in></p>

<p><pval>One sided <inp>p_1</inp></pval><br />
<pval>Two sided <inp>p_2</inp></pval></p>
<block name="warn">

<p><warn>WARNING: numbers too small for this test consider using a Student t test instead</warn></p>
</block>
</report>
